{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"95e6cd329d85b6fd","name":"card_unit_289th_gatchina","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/Homefront/units/card_unit_289th_gatchina","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"289th GATCHINA","text":"Destruction: Draw a card. Your HQ gains defense equal to its cost.","flavorText":"The 289th Rifle Regiment served as part of the 120th Rifle Division, a formation which saw extensive combat across several fronts in WWII. The division’s third and final formation was established in April 1943 and took part in the Leningrad-Novgorod Offensive, helping to liberate key areas from German control. For its role in the battle for Gatchina, the division received the city’s name as an honorific title. During the fighting around Leningrad, the 120th operated under difficult winter conditions and against fortified German positions. After breaking through the siege lines, it participated in operations pushing into Estonia, notably engaging in the Battle of Narva in 1944. As the war progressed, the division advanced westward with Soviet forces and was ultimately involved in the climactic Battle of Berlin. For its combat performance, the division was awarded the Order of the Red Banner.","faction":"Soviet","type":"infantry","rarity":"Unique","cost":2,"operationCost":2,"attack":5,"defense":2},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"GameplayTags":["ability.bond"],"Name":"card_unit_289th_gatchina","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_289th_gatchina_title","SourceString":"289th GATCHINA","LocalizedString":"289th GATCHINA"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":5,"defense":2,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_289th_gatchina_text","SourceString":"Destruction: Draw a card. Your HQ gains defense equal to its cost.","LocalizedString":"Destruction: Draw a card. Your HQ gains defense equal to its cost."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_2